Hello!
My name is Antonella and I'm PhD student from Argentina. I'm working with wild guanacos and I intend to use dsm in the data collected. I have 8 transects  (10km length each) surveyed during 3 different periods  (September, December and February) of the reproductive seasons of 2014 and 2016.  I'm interested in guanacos density in every period.  I was reading that one alternative is to pool all data from the 2 repeated visits in each period into a single line transect prior to analysis and to record the effort as transect length multiplied by 2 visits (in my case effort=20km). And for every period I should run a separate model.

-Is that alternative OK even though the visits are not close in time? Do I have to put this in an argument in the ds function?

-Should I do the same when I prepare the segments for dsm? So, in the same segment, I will have counts of the animals from, for example, September 2014 and 2016?

Thank you very much in advance!

